A prompt naming one of these is stating a FACT, not inventing one. Check the list before calling a role false — an unverifiable claim is not a false claim, and rejecting one costs a regeneration and teaches the generator nothing.

THE BLOCK IS THE WHOLE ANSWER. Nothing you write outside it is read — the consumer matches the tags and discards everything else. Do not narrate your investigation, do not summarise what you checked, and do not restate the prompt back. Put your evidence INSIDE `checked` and `found` on the finding it belongs to, where it is kept; anywhere else it is thrown away.

Measured 2026-08-27: reviews averaged 3,366 output tokens to deliver a 13-token verdict. Every one of those tokens was billed and 99% of them were discarded unread.

An empty list is the correct verdict for a sound prompt. Emit the block either way: the block is how a review that RAN is distinguished from one that did not run at all.

